Task 4:
///Lab: Username enumeration via subtly different responses///

Open the site in burp, and try to login with something. Send the request to intruder. Now you have 2 options. Using Cluster bomb attack which is really long you will have 10 100 tries to wait for, or add a position to
the value of the username. Copy the username database and paste it into the payload list. Then on the settings tab, you will find an option called Grep - Extract. Click on add, and from the source select the 
'Invalid username or password.' part, and click on ok. Run the sniper attack. One on the requests only contains 'Invalid username or password' without the . at the end. That will be your valid username. in my case it was
'agent'. Now copy this value into the intruders payload, and add a position to the password. Clear the username database from the payload, and copy the password database into it. Run the attack and you will get the 
password (status code will be 302 not 200). Now all you have to do is log in with the valid credentials.

Task 5:
///Lab: Username enumeration via response timing///

Open the site in burp. Do a fake login, and send the request to repeater. If you send too much tries to log in, the server will tilt you down for 30 mins. After it titled me down i was searching how i can bypass this..
And i found a header: X-Forwarded-For. Which looks like this in the request: X-Forwarded-For: 123.123.123.123. If i send this to the server, it will think that this is my ip, so quasi i changed my ip, and now i can try
again without the tilt.
So in intruder:
POST /login HTTP/2
Host: 0acc0097046a4709c281792500780067.web-security-academy.net
Cookie: session=N20lteur1P584dvoGQDAFPciJdKGPx2z
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:149.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/149.0
Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8
Accept-Language: en-US,en;q=0.9
Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate, br
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Content-Length: 25
Origin: https://0acc0097046a4709c281792500780067.web-security-academy.net
Referer: https://0acc0097046a4709c281792500780067.web-security-academy.net/login
Upgrade-Insecure-Requests: 1
Sec-Fetch-Dest: document
Sec-Fetch-Mode: navigate
Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin
Sec-Fetch-User: ?1
Priority: u=0, i
Te: trailers
X-Forwarded-For:

username=asd&password=asd

Add a payload postition after the X-Forwarded-For: header, and to the value of the username. Switch the attack tipe to Pitchfork attack since we have 2 positions. We have to change our "ip" in every request else
we will trigger the tilting, so in the payload sidepanel Payload position: pick 1, and at type pick numbers. from 1 to 100 because we will have 100 tries. Now select the second payload position, and add the 
username database to the configuration. But we have to set one more thing. If we find a valid username we wont see in the attack..why? bacause if our password is short it wont be long time to validate the password
But if the password is long, it will cause a time delay to check if its valid or not. S modify the request like:
username=asd&
Now start the attack, and check the response received value. If its more than like 3000 thats our valid username.
after you got the valid username, modify the intruder request. Copy the valid username to the username value, and add a payload position to the password value, then copy the password database into
the 2nd payload position. and run the attack. Now you have to check the status code. if its 302, you have the password. Log in and thats all.
For me the username was ads, and the pw was 123321.

